node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.git
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
*.log
# Next build output — every image runs its own `next build` in the builder stage, so a host .next is dead weight
# that also risks a stale artifact winning. Includes the NEXT_DIST_DIR variants a side-by-side dev server writes
# (.next-dev, .next-verify, …), which grow to tens of GB and otherwise ride into EVERY image's context.
.next
**/.next
**/.next-*
# Packaging artifacts (electron installers, CLI SEA bundle) — output of a build, never an input to one.
apps/desktop/release
apps/desktop/bundle
apps/cli/bundle
# Never bake env files (root + nested) into the image — secret leakage + Next loading a dev .env.local at
# runtime and changing behavior (e.g. keycloakConfigured). Inject runtime env only via compose `environment:`.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
